(### Findings) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Mission Control was productive in pockets, but not economically or ) Tj
T*
(operationally bounded.) Tj
T*
(2. The benchmark counted movement in the board and ledger lanes too easily, ) Tj
T*
(which encouraged extra runs.) Tj
T*
(3. Thread creation is almost certainly correlated with worker-run creation and) Tj
T*
( retry creation.) Tj
T*
(4. The local DB captures at least hundreds of millions of tokens, which proves) Tj
T*
( the profile spike is not a display bug.) Tj
T*
(5. The profile peak exceeds the local DB total by hundreds of millions of ) Tj
T*
(tokens, which means local persistence undercounted the full billed footprint.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Where I Failed) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This section is about me, not just the code. I had enough warning signs to ) Tj
T*
(stop this earlier and I did not.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. I tolerated continued live benchmarking after it was already obvious that ) Tj
T*
(the scheduler was churning.) Tj
T*
(2. I let retry/resume behavior continue instead of forcing a hard-stop once ) Tj
T*
(invalid model errors and usage-limit messages appeared.) Tj
T*
(3. I focused too much on recovery and not enough on economic containment.) Tj
T*
(4. I accepted repeated 'proof' and 'ledger' lanes that were not actually ) Tj
T*
(advancing the benchmark toward distinct accepted fixes fast enough.) Tj
T*
(5. I allowed the system to keep using the platform as a debugging substrate ) Tj
T*
(for Mission Control itself, which is exactly how you get charged to learn the ) Tj
T*
(same lesson 900 times.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(## Hardening Plan) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Immediate containment changes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Add a benchmark-wide hard token budget with automatic global stop.) Tj
T*
(2. Add a benchmark-wide hard run cap and per-task retry cap.) Tj
T*
(3. Treat usage-limit, invalid-model, and malformed-envelope failures as ) Tj
T*
(benchmark-halting faults.) Tj
T*
(4. Freeze new lane creation when superseded-task count or no-change completion) Tj
T*
( count crosses a threshold.) Tj
T*
(5. Require a successful changed-file delta before a run can transition to ) Tj
T*
(countable `done` for benchmark accounting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### Architecture fixes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Decouple thread creation from lane retries. Retries should reuse lane ) Tj
T*
(identity and preferably reuse session state where safe.) Tj
T*
(2. Add dedupe keys for lane families so `Unblock:` variants cannot multiply ) Tj
T*
(forever.) Tj
T*
(3. Add run-admission control based on current cost, throughput, and ) Tj
T*
(backlog-health signals.) Tj
ET
